# Commit between major changes

After each coherent unit of work — and after `npm run build` + `npm run playtest:smoke` (and full `npm run playtest` when required) pass — create a git commit before starting the next major change.

- Use conventional commits: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`
- Keep commits focused (one purpose each when practical)
- Do not accumulate large unrelated diffs
- Do not amend pushed commits unless explicitly asked
- Do not force-push or change git config
